---
// Debugging by conversation: swarm anomaly → translator explanation → human correction. Used in "The Answer Was Already in the Weights".
---

<figure class="diagram">
  <div class="steps">
    <div class="step">
      <p class="who">Swarm</p>
      <p class="raw">vector block #9821 · anomaly</p>
      <p class="note">A decision, in a language nobody reads</p>
    </div>
    <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
    <div class="step translator">
      <p class="who">Translator</p>
      <p>“I bypassed Protocol X because node Y showed a 94% latency risk.”</p>
    </div>
    <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
    <div class="step">
      <p class="who">You</p>
      <p>“Too cautious. Under these conditions, prioritize Protocol X.”</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="return">↺ The swarm adjusts its behavior. No code, no compile, no deploy.</p>
  <figcaption>
    You don't debug lines of code. You debug the reasoning, in words, at the level of concepts you
    and the machine both understand.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .steps {
    display: flex;
    align-items: stretch;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }
  .step {
    flex: 1;
    padding: 0.75rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    background: var(--surface-2);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }
  .step p {
    margin: 0;
  }
  .translator {
    border-color: var(--accent);
    background: var(--accent-soft);
  }
  .who {
    margin-bottom: 0.4rem !important;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-3);
  }
  .raw {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
  }
  .note {
    margin-top: 0.4rem !important;
    color: var(--text-3);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
  }
  .arrow {
    align-self: center;
    color: var(--text-3);
  }
  .return {
    margin: 0.75rem 0 0;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--text-2);
    text-align: center;
  }
  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .steps {
      flex-direction: column;
    }
    .arrow {
      transform: rotate(90deg);
    }
  }
</style>
